\n   344\tredundant `[gate-norm-beta-step 2]` (the `/1` body delegates) and\n   345\t`[gate-norm-beta-reduction 1]`. Companion F7b†\n   346\t`:h3-3-beta-step-binder` — `(quote (λ [x ✳] [(λ [y ✳] y) x]))` →\n   347\t`[(λ [x ✳] x) 1]`, the binder branch with the redex under the binder;\n   348\tsame traces, redundant for `/1`. Edge companion F7c†\n   349\t`:h3-3-beta-step-no-redex` — `(quote x)` → `[x 0]`: the no-reduction\n   350\tresult is a value, recorded here so integration does not mistake it for\n   351\ta refusal shape.\n   352\t\n   353\tF8† `:h3-3-beta-step-two` — primary witness for `beta-step/2` (direct):\n   354\t\n   355\t```clojure\n   356\t{:id :h3-3-beta-step-two,\n   357\t :call (latte-kernel.norm/beta-step (quote [(λ [x ✳] x) y]) 5)}\n   358\t```\n   359\t\n   360\tExpected A/B/C: `[y 6]` — the threaded count is observable, which is\n   361\twhat distinguishes `/2` from `/1` beyond the trace. Required trace:\n   362\t`[gate-norm-beta-step 2]`; redundant `[gate-norm-beta-reduction 1]`.\n   363\t\n   364\tF9† `:h3-3-beta-step-args` — primary witness for `beta-step-args/2`\n   365\t(direct):\n   366\t\n   367\t```clojure\n   368\t{:id :h3-3-beta-step-args,\n   369\t :call (latte-kernel.norm/beta-step-args (quote ([(λ [x ✳] x) y] z)) 0)}\n   370\t```\n   371\t\n   372\tExpected A/B/C: `[[y z] 1]` — one of the two parallel arguments\n   373\treduces; the count threads across both. Required trace:\n   374\t`[gate-norm-beta-step-args 2]`; redundant `[gate-norm-beta-step 2]`,\n   375\t`[gate-norm-beta-reduction 1]`.\n   376\t\n   377\t### 4.4 norm: instantiate-def\n   378\t\n   379\tF10† `:h3-3-norm-instantiate-def` — primary witness for\n   380\t`norm/instantiate-def/3` (direct), upstream's own\n   381\t`test-instantiate-def` full case:\n   382\t\n   383\t```clojure\n   384\t{:id :h3-3-norm-instantiate-def,\n   385\t :call (latte-kernel.norm/instantiate-def (quote [[x ✳] [y ✳] [z ✳]])\n   386\t                                          (quote [[x y] [z x]])