ons [(latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition (quote d) [] 0 (quote ✳) #{} (quote □) {})],\n   426\t :call (latte-kernel.norm/delta-step env [] (quote (d)) false)}\n   427\t```\n   428\t\n   429\tExpected A/B/C: `[✳ 1]`, same traces as F11. Keeping both rows pins the\n   430\tflag's two lookup scopes; a `local? true` call against a merely global\n   431\tdefinition throws `\"No such definition\"` and is **not** given a row —\n   432\tthat divergence risk (A's namespace fallback) is already recorded by\n   433\t`:entry-delta-local-namespace-shadow`, and duplicating it here would\n   434\tadd a boundary row, not coverage. The missing-definition refusal is R8.\n   435\t\n   436\tF12† `:h3-3-delta-step-args` — primary witness for\n   437\t`delta-step-args/5` (direct):\n   438\t\n   439\t```clojure\n   440\t{:id :h3-3-delta-step-args,\n   441\t :definitions [(latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition (quote d) [] 0 (quote ✳) #{} (quote □) {})],\n   442\t :call (latte-kernel.norm/delta-step-args env [] (quote ((d) [(λ [x ✳] x) y])) false 0)}\n   443\t```\n   444\t\n   445\tExpected A/B/C: `[[✳ [(λ [x ✳] x) y]] 1]` — the reference argument\n   446\tdelta-reduces (count 1), the application argument is stepped without\n   447\treducing (delta-step does not beta-reduce). Required trace:\n   448\t`[gate-norm-delta-step-args 5]`; redundant `[gate-norm-delta-step 5]`,\n   449\t`[gate-norm-delta-reduction 4]`, `[gate-norm-instantiate-def 3]`.\n   450\t\n   451\t### 4.6 presyntax and syntax\n   452\t\n   453\tF13† `:h3-3-parse-one` — primary witness for `parse/1` (direct):\n   454\t\n   455\t```clojure\n   456\t{:id :h3-3-parse-one,\n   457\t :call (latte-kernel.presyntax/parse (quote (lambda [x :type] x)))}\n   458\t```\n   459\t\n   460\tExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x ✳] x)`. Required trace:\n   461\t`[gate-presyntax-parse 1]`; redundant `[gate-presyntax-parse 2]` (the\n   462\t`/1` body delegates with the ambient environment, which the guest\n   463\trewrite supplies as its initial context). The two thrown refusals are\n   464\tR9. Existing `:parse-binder`/`:parse-application` rows cover `/2`; this\n   465\trow's only new content is the ambient-environment arity, which is\n   466\texactly the unexercised one.\n   467\t\n   468\tF14† `:h3-3-binderify` — primary witness for `binderify/3` (direct):\n   469\t\n   470\t```clojure\n   471\t{:id :h3-3-binderify,\n   472\t :call (latte-kernel.syntax/binderify (quote λ) (quote [[x ✳] [y A]]) (quote [x y]))}\n   473\t```\n   474\t\n   475\tExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x ✳] (λ [y A] [x y]))`. Required trace:\n   476\t`[gate-syntax-binderify 3]`, no redundant target traces. Companion\n   477\tF14b† `:h3-3-binderify-empty` — `(quote Π) (quote []) (quote B)` → `B`:\n   478\tzero bindings return the body; same trace, redundant for `/3`.\n   479\t\n   480\tF15† `:h3-3-mk-fresh-two` — primary witness for `mk-fresh/2` (direct):\n   481\t\n   482\t```clojure\n   483\t{:id :h3-3-mk-fresh-two,\n   484\t :call (latte-kernel.syntax/mk-fresh (quote x) (quote #{x x'}))}\n   485\t```\n   486\t\n   487\tExpected A/B/C: `x''`. Pure and deterministic (§3) — no supply is\n   488\tthreaded and no leg can disagree on freshness. Required trace:\n   489\t`[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`; redundant `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 3]` (the\n   490\t`/2` body delegates at level 0). Companion F15b†\n   491\t`:h3-3-mk-fresh-two-empty` — `(quote #{})` → `x`, the unforbidden base.\n   492\t\n   493\tF16† `:h3-3-mk-fresh-three` — primary witness for `mk-fresh/3`\n   494\t(direct), upstream's `test-mk-fresh` shape at an explicit level:\n   495\t\n   496\t```clojure\n   497\t{:id :h3-3-mk-fresh-three,\n   498\t :call (latte-kernel.syntax/mk-fresh (quote x) 3 (quote #{x x' x'' x'''}))}\n   499\t```\n   500\t\n   501\tExpected A/B/C: `x-4` — level 3's candidate `x'''` is forbidden, so the\n   502\tsearch continues to the numeric suffix. Required trace:\n   503\t`[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 3]` only. Companion F16b†\n   504\t`:h3-3-mk-fresh-three-level-zero` — level `0`, forbid `#{x}` → `x'`;\n   505\tsame trace, redundant for `/3`. The `^long` hint on the upstream level\n   506\tparameter is a host annotation; the guest receives the same integer\n   507\tliteral (precedent: numeric arguments in `:predicate-vectorn`).\n   508\t\n   509\tF17† `:h3-3-readable-term` — primary witness for `readable-term/1`\n   510\t(direct):\n   511\t\n   512\t```clojure\n   513\t{:id :h3-3-readable-term,\n   514\t :call (latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term (quote [(λ [x ✳] x) x]))}\n   515\t```\n   516\t\n   517\tExpected A/B/C: `[(λ [x' ✳] x') x]` — the bound `x` collides with the\n   518\tfree `x` and is renamed; the free occurrence is untouched. Required\n   519\ttrace: `[gate-syntax-readable-term 1]`; redundant\n   520\t`[gate-syntax-readable-term- 2]`, `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`,\n   521\t`[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`. Companion F17b† `:h3-3-readable-term-var` —\n   522\t`(quote x)` → `x` (no binder, identity). The metadata-named upstream\n   523\tcases are inexpressible in corpus EDN (§3) and are not attempted.\n   524\t\n   525\tF18† `:h3-3-readable-term-2` — primary witness for `readable-term-/2`\n   526\t(**named integration**, §7):\n   527\t\n   528\t```clojure\n   529\t{:id :h3-3-readable-term-2,\n   530\t :call ((var latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term-) (quote #{x}) (quote (λ [x ✳] x))),\n   531\t :guest-call (latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- (quote #{x}) (quote (λ [x ✳] x)))}\n   532\t```\n   533\t\n   534\tExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x' ✳] x')`. The `:call` reaches the private var\n   535\tthrough `(var …)` (a direct qualified call does not compile on the A\n   536\tleg — verified in this round); the `:guest-call` is the ordinary guest\n   537\tform, where the gate-compiled `readable-term-` is a plain definition.\n   538\tRequired trace: `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 2]` in both C lanes, plus\n   539\tredundant `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`, `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`.\n   540\tCredit requires registering `:h3-3-readable-term-2` in\n   541\t`kernel-named-integrations` at integration.\n   542\t\n   543\tF19† `:h3-3-readable-term-3` — primary witness for `readable-term-/3`\n   544\t(**named integration**):\n   545\t\n   546\t```clojure\n   547\t{:id :h3-3-readable-term-3,\n   548\t :call ((var latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term-) (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y]))),\n   549\t :guest-call (latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y])))}\n   550\t```\n   551\t\n   552\tExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x' ✳] [x' y])` — the explicit bound map is\n   553\tthreaded: the renamed binder is substituted for the bound occurrence,\n   554\tthe free `y` is untouched. Required trace:\n   555\t`[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`; redundant `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`.\n   556\tCredit requires registering `:h3-3-readable-term-3`, as F18.\n   557\t\n   558\t### 4.7 unparser (side-effecting)\n   559\t\n   560\tF20† `:h3-3-unregister-unparser` — primary witness for\n   561\t`unregister-unparser!/1` (**named integration**; the trace-name mapping\n   562\talready exists, §2):\n   563\t\n   564\t```clojure\n   565\t{:id :h3-3-unregister-unparser, :mode :unparser-install,\n   566\t :call (let [_ (latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n   567\t         [(latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x))\n   568\t          (do (latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! :gate)\n   569\t              (latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x)))]),\n   570\t :guest-call (let [k1 (register-unparser env :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
