direct |\n   105\t| `norm/beta-step 1` | `[gate-norm-beta-step 1]` | direct |\n   106\t| `norm/beta-step 2` | `[gate-norm-beta-step 2]` | direct |\n   107\t| `norm/beta-step-args 2` | `[gate-norm-beta-step-args 2]` | direct |\n   108\t| `norm/delta-step 4` | `[gate-norm-delta-step 4]` | direct |\n   109\t| `norm/delta-step-args 5` | `[gate-norm-delta-step-args 5]` | direct |\n   110\t| `norm/instantiate-def 3` | `[gate-norm-instantiate-def 3]` | direct |\n   111\t| `norm/redex? 1` | `[gate-norm-redex? 1]` | direct |\n   112\t| `presyntax/parse 1` | `[gate-presyntax-parse 1]` | direct; the body's ambient `empty-env` becomes the guest initial context |\n   113\t| `syntax/binderify 3` | `[gate-syntax-binderify 3]` | direct |\n   114\t| `syntax/mk-fresh 2` | `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]` | direct |\n   115\t| `syntax/mk-fresh 3` | `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 3]` | direct |\n   116\t| `syntax/readable-term 1` | `[gate-syntax-readable-term 1]` | direct |\n   117\t| `syntax/readable-term- 2` | `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 2]` | named integration (private var, §4.6) |\n   118\t| `syntax/readable-term- 3` | `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]` | named integration (private var, §4.6) |\n   119\t| `unparser/unregister-unparser! 1` | `[unregister-unparser 2]` | bare context name + 1; mapping already in the harness tables |\n   120\t\n   121\t## 3. Call graph the predictions rest on\n   122\t\n   123\tFrom the pinned sources:\n   124\t\n   125\t- `defenv/axiom?/1` (`defenv.cljc:177`) is `instance? Axiom`. The context\n   126\t  adaptation replaces records with `:latte/kind` maps and the predicate\n   127\t  with a kind check (`context.edn`), so a `->Axiom` construction agrees\n   128\t  on A (record) and B/C (map) with outcome `true`; a `Definition` and a\n   129\t  plain map both give `false`.\n   130\t- `defenv/registered-definition?` (`defenv.cljc:99`) is multi-arity:\n   131\t  `/1` means `(registered-definition? empty-env dname false)` — the\n   132\t  ambient environment. The context adaptation\n   133\t  (`context.edn:56`) has no ambient form; its arities are\n   134\t  `[kernel dname]` and `[kernel dname local?]`, i.e. upstream `/2` and\n   135\t  `/3` shifted by the explicit context. The gate wrapper the harness\n   136\t  generates for `/1` therefore delegates `(registered-definition? p0)`\n   137\t  to a context function that requires the context first — an arity\n   138\t  error on B/C (§7). Upstream `/1` itself never throws for a symbol: an\n   139\t  unregistered, unresolvable name fetches `[:ko …]` and yields `false`\n   140\t  (`defenv.cljc:81`); a non-symbol name throws\n   141\t  `\"Cannot fetch definition (please report)\" {:dname …}`\n   142\t  (`defenv.cljc:96`).\n   143\t- `nbe/evaluation` (`nbe.cljc:87`): `/1` delegates to the 4-arity with\n   144\t  `{}` function environment, `empty-env`, `[]` context. On a binder the\n   145\t  result **embeds a host Clojure function** (`nbe.cljc:102`), which is\n   146\t  nonportable evidence (a host `fn` on A/B, a guest closure on C; the\n   147\t  harness's `evidence-data` marks it `:nonportable-host-value`). Fixture\n   148\t  terms must therefore fully apply, reducing to plain data: a redex\n   149\t  `[(λ [a ✳] a) b]` evaluates to the symbol `b` and never returns a\n   150\t  binder. A reference to a missing definition throws\n   151\t  `\"No such definition\" {:term t :def-name name}` via `delta-reduction`\n   152\t  (`nbe.cljc:44`).\n   153\t- `nbe/instantiate-def/3` (`nbe.cljc:25`): `binderify`s the parameters\n   154\t  over the body, then folds the arguments on as vector applications; it\n   155\t  does **not** substitute. More arguments than parameters throws\n   156\t  `\"Not enough parameters (please report)\" {:args args}` with the\n   157\t  **original** argument vector (`nbe.cljc:29`). Contrast\n   158\t  `norm/instantiate-def/3` (`norm.cljc:229`), which substitutes via\n   159\t  `stx/subst`, re-abstracts unfilled parameters (renaming on collision —\n   160\t  the partial case yields `t'` for `t`), and throws the same message\n   161\t  with the **remaining** argument sequence (`norm.cljc:238`). The two\n   162\t  functions share a name and a message; the fixtures must not conflate\n   163\t  their expected data.\n   164\t- `norm/redex?/1` (`norm.cljc:88`): application whose first element is a\n   165\t  `λ`. `norm/beta-reduction/1` (`norm.cljc:94`) substitutes the argument\n   166\t  for the bound variable and throws\n   167\t  `\"Cannot beta-reduce. Not a redex\" {:term t}` otherwise.\n   168\t- `norm/beta-step` (`norm.cljc:116`): `/1` is `(beta-step t 0)`; `/2`\n   169\t  threads the reduction count. The application branch recurs through\n   170\t  `beta-reduction` (hence every successful `beta-step` fixture also\n   171\t  traces `beta-reduction/1`); the reference branch goes through\n   172\t  `beta-step-args/2` (`norm.cljc:164`), which steps each argument with\n   173\t  the threaded count. A term with no redex returns `[t 0]` — a value,\n   174\t  not a refusal.\n   175\t- `norm/delta-step` (`norm.cljc:321`): arities `/3` (already exercised),\n   176\t  `/4` (`local?`, the target), `/5` (internal, already exercised). The\n   177\t  reference branch calls `delta-reduction` (which calls\n   178\t  `norm/instantiate-def/3` when unfolding) and recurs at `/5` while\n   179\t  reductions happen; a non-reducible reference steps its arguments via\n   180\t  `delta-step-args/5` (`norm.cljc:375`). Environment threading is the\n   181\t  point of `/4`: `local? true` fetches with `local-only?` (a globally\n   182\t  registered definition then throws `\"No such definition\"`), `local?\n   183\t  false` also sees globals. Upstream fetch on A additionally falls back\n   184\t  to namespace resolution; every fixture here registers its definition\n   185\t  explicitly in the environment, so that fallback is never consulted\n   186\t  and A/B/C cannot diverge on it (the guest has no namespace fallback —\n   187\t  cf. the existing `:entry-delta-local-namespace-shadow` boundary).\n   188\t- `presyntax/parse/1` (`presyntax.cljc:95`): `(parse empty-env t)`; a\n   189\t  `[:ko …]` from `parse-term` is rethrown as ex-info `\"Parse error\"`\n   190\t  carrying the parse-error map. The ambient `empty-env` is exactly what\n   191\t  the harness's guest rewrite replaces with the initial context.\n   192\t- `syntax/binderify/3` (`syntax.cljc:57`): folds bindings in reverse\n   193\t  over the body; zero bindings return the body unchanged.\n   194\t- `syntax/mk-fresh` (`syntax.cljc:262`): `/2` is `(mk-fresh base 0\n   195\t  forbid)`; `/3` tries suffixes `\"\"`, `'`, `''`, `'''`, then `-4`,\n   196\t  `-5`, … by level. It is **pure**: it builds a symbol from the base\n   197\t  name and the level; there is no gensym and no fresh-supply counter\n   198\t  involved (contrast `typing/rebuild-type`, whose supply the harness\n   199\t  threads explicitly). Repeated calls with equal arguments return equal\n   200\t  symbols on every leg, so no freshness side condition is needed; the\n   201\t  design corrects the brief's \"gensym freshness\" framing here.\n   202\t- `syntax/readable-term/1` (`syntax.cljc:478`) computes the free\n   203\t  variables and delegates to the private `readable-term-`\n   204\t  (`syntax.cljc:449`): `/2` supplies an empty bound map, `/3` threads\n   205\t  `free`/`bound`. A bound variable whose name occurs in `free` is\n   206\t  renamed with `mk-fresh/2` (no metadata case: `(:name (meta x) x)`\n   207\t  defaults to the symbol itself — corpus EDN cannot carry `with-meta`\n   208\t  symbols, so the metadata-named cases in upstream's\n   209\t  `test-readable-term` are not expressible as corpus rows and are out of\n   210\t  scope; the collision renaming they exercise is reproduced with plain\n   211\t  symbols). Two consequences: (a) `readable-term-` is a `defn-`, so the\n   212\t  A leg cannot eval a direct qualified call to it (compile error:\n   213\t  var is not public); the corpus `:call` must use the `(var …)` form,\n   214\t  which also means the call head is not the function symbol and direct\n   215\t  credit is impossible (§7); (b) the body calls `meta`, which the guest\n   216\t  library must serve — precedent exists (`:minimal-with-meta`), flagged\n   217\t  as the one library-dependency risk in §8.\n   218\t- `unparser/unregister-unparser!/1` (`unparser.cljc:29`): mutates the\n   219\t  ambient `+unparser-registry+` atom; throws `\"No such unparser.\"\n   220\t  {:ident ident}` when the ident is absent. The context adaptation\n   221\t  threads an immutable registry through an explicit context\n   222\t  (`context.edn:92`), and the harness already maps the trace name\n   223\t  (`unregister-unparser`, +1 argument). The A leg isolates the atom via\n   224\t  the existing `:unparser-install` mode, so no fixture here mutates\n   225\t  shared upstream state beyond that isolation. **Conservative-upstream\n   226\t  note (binding):** `unparser.cljc:35` rebuilds the `:user` list from\n   227\t  the `:standard` list (`(u/vremove #(= % ident) (:standard registry))`)\n   228\t  — unregistering a `:user` ident replaces `:user` with the filtered\n   229\t  `:standard` list. The context source preserves this exactly\n   230\t  (`context.edn:99`, \"Preserve the upstream unregister's\n   231\t  :user-from-:standard behavior exactly\"). No fixture may expect the\n   232\t  corrected `:user` list; the A-verification script pins the upstream\n   233\t  registry shape for this case, and §4.7's fixture observes the effect\n   234\t  only through `unparse`, which is insensitive to it for a single\n   235\t  registered ident.\n   236\t\n   237\t## 4. The family\n   238\t\n   239\tProposed corpus rows are shown in the corpus's EDN shape (A form; the\n   240\tharness derives B/C, using `:guest-call` where present). New IDs are\n   241\tmarked †. Every predicted A outcome below is A-verified (§0); predicted\n   242\tB/C outcomes are the same value unless stated, derived per §3.\n   243\t\n   244\t### 4.1 defenv predicates\n   245\t\n   246\tF1† `:h3-3-axiom-true` — primary witness for `axiom?/1` (direct):\n   247\t\n   248\t```clojure\n   249\t{:id :h3-3-axiom-true,\n   250\t :call (latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? (latte-kernel.defenv/->Axiom (quote a) [] 0 (quote T)))}\n   251\t```\n   252\t\n   253\tExpected A/B/C: `true`. Required trace: `[gate-defenv-axiom? 1]` in both\n   254\tC lanes. The two false companions are refusal rows in §5 (R1); they trace\n   255\tthe same record but, as `:negative?` rows, confer nothing.\n   256\t\n   257\tF2† `:h3-3-registered-definition-ambient` — primary witness for\n   258\t`registered-definition?/1`, **conditional** (§7):\n   259\t\n   260\t```clojure\n   261\t{:id :h3-3-registered-definition-ambient,\n   262\t :call (latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? (quote gate-no-such-definition)),\n   263\t :guest-call (registered-definition? env (quote gate-no-such-definition))}\n   264\t```\n   265\t\n   266\tExpected A: `false` — the name is in neither the ambient `empty-env`\n   267\tnor any namespace the A leg can resolve (the name is chosen to resolve\n   268\tnowhere; if a future namespace interns it, this prediction breaks and\n   269\tthe fixture must be renamed, never re-expected). Expected B/C: `false`\n   270\t(context fetch on the initial context misses both maps). Required trace\n   271\tfor credit: `[registered-definition? 2]` in both C lanes — creditable\n   272\t**only** if the integration round adds the trace-name registration of\n   273\t§7; under the harness as it stands this row is an honest pass that\n   274\tcredits nothing (the gate-wrapper `/1` it would otherwise use is\n   275\tarity-broken against the context signature, §3). The non-symbol refusal\n   276\tcompanion is R2 in §5. A `true` case for `/1` is deliberately **not**\n   277\tdesigned: on A it could only be produced by namespace resolution (the\n   278\tambient env is empty by definition), which B/C expressly do not have —\n   279\tsuch a row would be a manufactured mismatch, not a fixture.\n   280\t\n   281\t### 4.2 nbe\n   282\t\n   283\tF3† `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-one` — primary witness for `evaluation/1`\n   284\t(direct):\n   285\t\n   286\t```clojure\n   287\t{:id :h3-3-nbe-evaluation-one,\n   288\t :call (latte-kernel.nbe/evaluation (quote [(λ [a ✳] a) b]))}\n   289\t```\n   290\t\n   291\tExpected A/B/C: `b`. The term fully applies, so the host function the\n   292\tbinder branch builds is consumed internally and never appears in the\n   293\tresult (§3); a binder-returning term would embed a host `fn` and is\n   294\texcluded by design. Required trace: `[gate-nbe-evaluation 1]`, plus\n   295\tredundant `[gate-nbe-evaluation 4]`. Companion `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-var`\n   296\t(`(quote a)` → `a`, same traces) is a redundant second direct row; the\n   297\tmissing-reference refusal is R3.\n   298\t\n   299\tF4† `:h3-3-nbe-instantiate-def` — primary witness for\n   300\t`nbe/instantiate-def/3` (direct):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
