g — verified in this round); the `:guest-call` is the ordinary guest\n   537\tform, where the gate-compiled `readable-term-` is a plain definition.\n   538\tRequired trace: `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 2]` in both C lanes, plus\n   539\tredundant `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`, `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`.\n   540\tCredit requires registering `:h3-3-readable-term-2` in\n   541\t`kernel-named-integrations` at integration.\n   542\t\n   543\tF19† `:h3-3-readable-term-3` — primary witness for `readable-term-/3`\n   544\t(**named integration**):\n   545\t\n   546\t```clojure\n   547\t{:id :h3-3-readable-term-3,\n   548\t :call ((var latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term-) (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y]))),\n   549\t :guest-call (latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- (quote #{x}) (quote {}) (quote (λ [x ✳] [x y])))}\n   550\t```\n   551\t\n   552\tExpected A/B/C: `(λ [x' ✳] [x' y])` — the explicit bound map is\n   553\tthreaded: the renamed binder is substituted for the bound occurrence,\n   554\tthe free `y` is untouched. Required trace:\n   555\t`[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]`; redundant `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]`.\n   556\tCredit requires registering `:h3-3-readable-term-3`, as F18.\n   557\t\n   558\t### 4.7 unparser (side-effecting)\n   559\t\n   560\tF20† `:h3-3-unregister-unparser` — primary witness for\n   561\t`unregister-unparser!/1` (**named integration**; the trace-name mapping\n   562\talready exists, §2):\n   563\t\n   564\t```clojure\n   565\t{:id :h3-3-unregister-unparser, :mode :unparser-install,\n   566\t :call (let [_ (latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n   567\t         [(latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x))\n   568\t          (do (latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! :gate)\n   569\t              (latte-kernel.unparser/unparse (quote x)))]),\n   570\t :guest-call (let [k1 (register-unparser env :gate (fn [t] (if (= t (quote x)) [(quote shown) true] [t false])))]\n   571\t               [(unparse k1 (quote x)) (unparse (unregister-unparser k1 :gate) (quote x))])}\n   572\t```\n   573\t\n   574\tExpected A/B/C: `[shown x]` — before removal the registered unparser\n   575\trewrites `x`; after removal it does not. The effect is observed only\n   576\tthrough `unparse`, never through the registry value (which holds host\n   577\tfunctions upstream and guest closures on C — incomparable evidence by\n   578\tconstruction). The A leg runs under `:unparser-install`, so the ambient\n   579\tatom it mutates is the harness's isolated one; B/C thread the immutable\n   580\tregistry through the returned context, and the *prior* context is never\n   581\treused after removal in this row (prior-context preservation for\n   582\tregistries is already asserted by the slice-8 registry sequences).\n   583\tRequired trace: `[unregister-unparser 2]` in both C lanes; redundant\n   584\t`[register-unparser 3]`, `[unparse 2]`. Credit requires registering\n   585\t`:h3-3-unregister-unparser` in `kernel-named-integrations`; the\n   586\tconservative `:user`-from-`:standard` behavior (§3) is pinned on A by\n   587\tthe verification script and must not be \"corrected\" in any row. The\n   588\tabsent-ident refusal is R10.\n   589\t\n   590\t## 5. Refusal and edge companions (all `:negative? true` when integrated)\n   591\t\n   592\tNone of these confers credit. Expected A outcomes are A-verified;\n   593\tB/C are predicted to agree (thrown ex-info message+data, or the false\n   594\tvalue — the gate's negative check accepts thrown, `false`, or\n   595\t`:ko`-headed A outcomes).\n   596\t\n   597\t| ID | Fixture `:call` (guest form where it differs) | Expected A |\n   598\t|---|---|---|\n   599\t| R1† `:h3-3-axiom-definition` | `(latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? (latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition (quote d) [] 0 (quote body) #{} (quote T) {}))` | `false` |\n   600\t| R1† `:h3-3-axiom-map` | `(latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? {})` | `false` |\n   601\t| R2† `:h3-3-registered-definition-nonsymbol` | `(latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 5)`; guest `(registered-definition? env 5)` | thrown `\"Cannot fetch definition (please report)\" {:dname 5}` |\n   602\t| R3† `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-missing` | `(latte-kernel.nbe/evaluation (quote (gate-missing)))` | thrown `\"No such definition\" {:term (gate-missing) :def-name gate-missing}` |\n   603\t| R4† `:h3-3-nbe-instantiate-def-too-many` | `(latte-kernel.nbe/instantiate-def (quote [[x ✳]]) (quote x) (quote [a b]))` | thrown `\"Not enough parameters (please report)\" {:args [a b]}` |\n   604\t| R5† `:h3-3-redex-application` | `(latte-kernel.norm/redex? (quote [x y]))` | `false` |\n   605\t| R5† `:h3-3-redex-variable` | `(latte-kernel.norm/redex? (quote x))` | `false` |\n   606\t| R6† `:h3-3-beta-reduction-nonredex` | `(latte-kernel.norm/beta-reduction (quote [x y]))` | thrown `\"Cannot beta-reduce. Not a redex\" {:term [x y]}` |\n   607\t| R7† `:h3-3-norm-instantiate-def-too-many` | `(latte-kernel.norm/instantiate-def (quote [[x ✳]]) (quote x) (quote [a b]))` | thrown `\"Not enough parameters (please report)\" {:args (b)}` |\n   608\t| R8† `:h3-3-delta-step-missing` | `(latte-kernel.norm/delta-step env [] (quote (gate-missing)) false)` | thrown `\"No such definition\" {:term (gate-missing) :def-name gate-missing}` |\n   609\t| R9† `:h3-3-parse-one-empty` | `(latte-kernel.presyntax/parse (quote ()))` | thrown `\"Parse error\" {:msg \"Compound term is empty\" :term ()}` |\n   610\t| R9† `:h3-3-parse-one-reserved` | `(latte-kernel.presyntax/parse (quote lambda))` | thrown `\"Parse error\" {:msg \"Symbol is reserved\" :term lambda}` |\n   611\t| R10† `:h3-3-unregister-unparser-absent` | `:mode :unparser-install`, `(latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! :absent)`; guest `(unregister-unparser env :absent)` | thrown `\"No such unparser.\" {:ident :absent}` |\n   612\t\n   613\tR4 vs R7 is the pair most likely to be mis-transcribed at integration:\n   614\tsame message, different