eds the\n   647\tID added to `kernel-named-integrations`; conditional needs that plus\n   648\tthe trace-name registration below. Redundant witnesses trace the arity\n   649\ttoo (predicted, §4) but no credit in this accounting rests on them.\n   650\t\n   651\t| Arity | Primary fixture | Credit kind | Required trace (both C lanes) |\n   652\t|---|---|---|---|\n   653\t| `defenv/axiom? 1` | F1 `:h3-3-axiom-true` | direct | `[gate-defenv-axiom? 1]` |\n   654\t| `defenv/registered-definition? 1` | F2 `:h3-3-registered-definition-ambient` | **conditional** | `[registered-definition? 2]` |\n   655\t| `nbe/evaluation 1` | F3 `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-one` | direct | `[gate-nbe-evaluation 1]` |\n   656\t| `nbe/instantiate-def 3` | F4 `:h3-3-nbe-instantiate-def` | direct | `[gate-nbe-instantiate-def 3]` |\n   657\t| `norm/redex? 1` | F5 `:h3-3-redex-true` | direct | `[gate-norm-redex? 1]` |\n   658\t| `norm/beta-reduction 1` | F6 `:h3-3-beta-reduction` | direct | `[gate-norm-beta-reduction 1]` |\n   659\t| `norm/beta-step 1` | F7 `:h3-3-beta-step-one` | direct | `[gate-norm-beta-step 1]` |\n   660\t| `norm/beta-step 2` | F8 `:h3-3-beta-step-two` | direct | `[gate-norm-beta-step 2]` |\n   661\t| `norm/beta-step-args 2` | F9 `:h3-3-beta-step-args` | direct | `[gate-norm-beta-step-args 2]` |\n   662\t| `norm/instantiate-def 3` | F10 `:h3-3-norm-instantiate-def` | direct | `[gate-norm-instantiate-def 3]` |\n   663\t| `norm/delta-step 4` | F11 `:h3-3-delta-step-four-local` | direct | `[gate-norm-delta-step 4]` |\n   664\t| `norm/delta-step-args 5` | F12 `:h3-3-delta-step-args` | direct | `[gate-norm-delta-step-args 5]` |\n   665\t| `presyntax/parse 1` | F13 `:h3-3-parse-one` | direct | `[gate-presyntax-parse 1]` |\n   666\t| `syntax/binderify 3` | F14 `:h3-3-binderify` | direct | `[gate-syntax-binderify 3]` |\n   667\t| `syntax/mk-fresh 2` | F15 `:h3-3-mk-fresh-two` | direct | `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 2]` |\n   668\t| `syntax/mk-fresh 3` | F16 `:h3-3-mk-fresh-three` | direct | `[gate-syntax-mk-fresh 3]` |\n   669\t| `syntax/readable-term 1` | F17 `:h3-3-readable-term` | direct | `[gate-syntax-readable-term 1]` |\n   670\t| `syntax/readable-term- 2` | F18 `:h3-3-readable-term-2` | named-integration | `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 2]` |\n   671\t| `syntax/readable-term- 3` | F19 `:h3-3-readable-term-3` | named-integration | `[gate-syntax-readable-term- 3]` |\n   672\t| `unparser/unregister-unparser! 1` | F20 `:h3-3-unregister-unparser` | named-integration | `[unregister-unparser 2]` |\n   673\t\n   674\tHonest accounting, by credit kind:\n   675\t\n   676\t- **16 arities credit by ordinary direct fixtures** as the harness\n   677\t  stands today (F1, F3–F17 minus the named ones): no registration, no\n   678\t  harness change. If any one's trace is missing from a passing row at\n   679\t  integration (e.g. the guest compiler refuses a shape), that arity\n   680\t  stays unexercised and the plan's residual rule applies — add a\n   681\t  minimal helper fixture, never weaken the trace rule.\n   682\t- **3 arities credit as named integrations** (F18, F19, F20): the\n   683\t  fixture shapes are corpus-supported today (`:guest-call`, `:mode`),\n   684\t  but credit lands only when integration registers the three IDs in\n   685\t  `kernel-named-integrations`. F20's trace-name mapping already exists;\n   686\t  F18/F19 need only the ID registration.\n   687\t- **1 arity cannot be credited by an ordinary fixture**:\n   688\t  `defenv/registered-definition?/1`. Reason: upstream `/1` is the\n   689\t  ambient-`empty-env` form; the context adaptation has no ambient form,\n   690\t  so (a) the generated gate wrapper for `/1` delegates one argument to\n   691\t  a context function whose first argument is the context — an arity\n   692\t  error on B/C, hence `:blocked`, never `:pass`; and (b) the bare\n   693\t  context trace `[registered-definition? 2]` that F2's `:guest-call`\n   694\t  does produce is not mapped to this symbol in\n   695\t  `kernel-context-integration-names` / `kernel-context-extra-arguments`\n   696\t  as the harness stands. The remedy is small and precedented — add\n   697\t  `'latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 'registered-definition?`\n   698\t  to `kernel-context-integration-names` and `'registered-definition? 1`\n   699\t  to `kernel-context-extra-arguments`, exactly the treatment\n   700\t  `unregister-unparser!` already has — but it is a harness-table change,\n   701\t  so it belongs to the reviewed integration round, not to an ordinary\n   702\t  fixture. **Until that registration lands, F2 is an honest passing row\n   703\t  that credits nothing, and the gate stays `:blocked` on this one\n   704\t  arity.** This is the only one of the 20 in that position.\n   705\t- No arity is left without a designed fixture or an explicit note:\n   706\t  16 direct + 3 named-integration + 1 conditional = 20.\n   707\t- Preparation contributes **zero** coverage until reviewed and\n   708\t  integrated: nothing in this round changes the checked-in evidence,\n   709\t  and the gate remains `:blocked` with 20 unexercised arities.\n   710\t\n   711\tRedundant (incidental) witnesses, predicted from §3's call graph —\n   712\tuseful if a primary trace is missing at integration, never counted\n   713\tabove: `binderify/3` also in F4; `beta-reduction/1`, `beta-step/2`,\n   714\t`redex?/1` also across F6–F9; `norm/instantiate-def/3` also in F11/F12\n   715\t(via `delta-reduction`); `mk-fresh/2`, `mk-fresh/3`,\n   716\t`readable-term-/2`, `readable-term-/3` also across F15/F17/F18;\n   717\t`parse/2` in F13 (already credited elsewhere).\n   718\t\n   719\t## 8. Integration sketch and verification (next round, not this one)\n   720\t\n   721\tA-verification, before any harness edit:\n   722\t\n   723\t```sh\n   724\tclj -M:test -e \"(do (load-file \\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_a_verify.clj\\\") (yang.latte-oracle.h3-3-a-verify/-main))\"\n   725\t```\n   726\t\n   727\tExpected: `H3-3-A-VERIFY: PASS (43/43)`, exit 0. Any `FAIL` revises the\n   728\tmatching prediction above first (document + script together), never the\n   729\tother way round. This round ran the script with the equivalent\n   730\texplicit-classpath invocation\n   731\t(`clj -Sdeps '{:paths [\"test\" \"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\"] :deps\n   732\t{latte-kernel/latte-kernel {:git/url\n   733\t\"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\" :git/sha\n   734\t\"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}}' -M -e \"…\"`), because on\n   735\tthis laptop the `:test` alias's test-runner main also loads every test\n   736\tnamespace and fails on the ungenerated ANTLR parser classes\n   737\t(`yang.python.antlr.gen.Python3Lexer`) before reaching the script —\n   738\tan environment gap, not a script failure. Observed output: 43 `PASS`\n   739\tlines and `H3-3-A-VERIFY: PASS (43/43)`, exit 0.\n   740\t\n   741\tIntegration (after design review; exact harness edits for the\n   742\tintegration engineer):\n   743\t\n   744\t1. Add the §4/§5 rows to `kernel_gate.edn` (F1–F20 primaries and\n   745\t   companions, then R1–R10 as `:negative? true` rows; one row per case\n   746\t   where a group above lists two calls).\n   747\t2. Register `:h3-3-readable-term-2`, `:h3-3-readable-term-3`, and\n   748\t   `:h3-3-unregister-unparser` in `kernel-named-integrations`.\n   749\t3. Decide the conditional (§7): either add the two\n   750\t   `registered-definition?` entries to\n   751\t   `kernel-context-integration-names` / `kernel-context-extra-arguments`\n   752\t   (recommended — precedented by `unregister-unparser`, and it is the\n   753\t   only path that can ever credit this arity), or land F2 as a\n   754\t   non-crediting pass and keep the gate honestly `:blocked` on\n   755\t   `registered-definition?/1` with the reason recorded here.\n   756\t4. No declarations change is expected: no fixture here is a recorded\n   757\t   deviation or upstream failure — every row is an ordinary `:pass` or\n   758\t   `:negative?` row — so `slice9_declarations.edn` should carry forward\n   759\t   unchanged unless integration discovers otherwise (if it does, that\n   760\t   discovery is a finding, not a silent edit).\n   761\t5. Run the focused gate test, refresh evidence with\n   762\t   `write-kernel-gate-evidence!`, and audit that every §7 primary\n   763\t   re-derives from both C-lane traces; publish credited/withdrawn/\n   764\t   remaining sets with fixture IDs. Expected after state if all rows\n   765\t   pass and step 3 lands: 165/165 exercised and the gate's\n   766\t   `:gate-status` assertion becomes satisfiable — that claim belongs\n   767\t   to the integration round's measured evidence, not to this document.\n   768\t\n   769\tRisks flagged for integration (predicted, not observed):\n   770\t\n   771\t- F17–F19's guest path calls `meta` (in `readable-term-`). The guest\n   772\t  library already serves `with-meta` (`:minimal-with-meta`), but if\n   773\t  bare `meta` on a symbol is not served, those three rows block at\n   774\t  admission/compile — the arity then stays unexercised and the\n   775\t  residual rule applies.\n   776\t- F2's A prediction depends on `gate-no-such-definition` resolving in\n   777\t  no namespace visible to the A leg (§4.1). The integration round\n   778\t  should keep that exact name and re-check if it ever fails.\n   779\t- F11's composed registration call must survive `kernel-call` rewriting\n   780\t  (precedent `:entry-delta-local` says it does); F12's quoted argument\n   781\t  list `((d) [(λ [x ✳] x) y])` mixes a reference and an application —\n   782\t  if the guest admission rejects either shape, split F12 into two rows\n   783\t  stepping one argument each rather than weakening the call.\n   784\t\n   785\tOpen questions for the design reviewer:\n   786\t\n   787\t- Is the §7 conditional registration (step 3) acceptable as a harness\n   788\t  table change in the integration round, or should\n   789\t  `registered-definition?/1` be recorded as a permanent honest\n   790\t  `:blocked` remainder with F2 landed as a non-crediting pass?\n   791\t- Should F20's registry-shape consequence (§6.1) also be pinned as a\n   792\t  B/C state assertion at integration (the slice-8 registry-replay\n   793\t  already snapshots it), or is A-side pinning plus the `unparse`\n   794\t  outcome sufficient?\n   795\t- F7b/F7c, F10b, F11b, F14b, F15b, F16b, F17b and\n   796\t  `:h3-3-nbe-evaluation-var` are redundant companions: integrate them\n   797\t  all (branch/edge evidence), or only the primaries plus §5? This\n   798\t  design recommends integrating them — witnesses that exist only in a\n   799\t  document do not survive compiler changes — but they are severable\n   800\t  without touching any primary credit.\n   801\t\n   802\t\n   803\t\n   804\t\n   805\t\n   806\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
